title: $:/plugins/nikorion/theme/language/en-GB/readme
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

A personal look for a TiddlyWiki: the author's stylesheets and the overrides of third-party shadow tiddlers (Vanilla theme settings, Kookma plugins, core custom properties), gathered in one plugin instead of being scattered as loose tiddlers of the wiki.

! What it changes

|!Part |!Tiddlers |
|Body text |`$:/nikorion/styles/body-text.css`: foreground and background colours, Inter font, no ligatures in code |
|Headings |`$:/nikorion/styles/headings.css`: Palatino headings with rules, site title |
|Rules |`$:/nikorion/styles/hr.css`: `<hr>` with a central logo (logo shipped with the plugin) |
|Code highlighting |`$:/nikorion/styles/highlight.css`: Obsidian colours for highlight.js |
|Frames |`$:/nikorion/styles/layoutVanilla.css`: tiddler frame and sidebar borders |
|Coloured blocks |`$:/nikorion/styles/infobox.css`: `info0`, `interro0`, `alert0` classes |
|Vanilla settings |font families, sizes, sidebar width, background image, sticky titles |
|Third-party overrides |Kookma Refnotes footnote counter, Kookma Tweaks headings (emptied), Shiraz Formatter highlight colours, core `custom-properties` |

! Loading order

The plugin declares `plugin-priority` 100. TiddlyWiki registers the shadow tiddlers of plugins in ascending priority, the last one winning: the core has 0, ordinary plugins and themes 1, so this plugin always overrides them, whatever their alphabetical order.

! Requirements

* TiddlyWiki >= 5.3.5.
* The fonts //Inter//, //Palatino Linotype// and //JetBrains Mono// are not shipped: install them on the machine or with the Font Manager plugin.
